Put the @vermicelli rice noodles{125%g} in a bowl, and tip boiling water over until covered. Leave for 30 to ~{45%seconds} until softened, but not soft, then drain. Leave to dry in a sieve or colander for about ~{30%minutes}, tossing occasionally to make sure they do not clump together.

Blanch the @green beans{handful} in boiling water, then drain and set aside. Add half the @curry powder{2.5%tsp} and all the @soy sauce{3%tbsp}, @rice wine or dry sherry{2%tbsp}, and @sugar{pinch}. Toss together well until the noodles are well coated.

Prepare the other ingredients in four separate bowls:\
• Garlic and ginger: @garlic{2%cloves}(crushed), @ginger{1%tbsp}(peeled and grated), @bird's eye green chilli{1}(finely chopped), @spring onions{2}(sliced on the diagonal), and remaining curry powder.\
• Vegetables: @water chestnuts{6}(sliced), @red pepper{0.5}(thinly sliced), @shiitake mushrooms{5}(sliced), and @peas{handful}\
• Meat and prawns: @char siu pork or cooked chicken{50%g}(shredded) and @prawns{50%g}.\
• Egg: @egg{1}(beaten with a pinch of salt and splash of sesame oil).

Heat the @peanut or other neutral oil{2%tbsp} in a #wok until smoking, then tip in the garlic and ginger mixture. Stir-fry for ~{30%seconds} until fragrant, then tip in the vegetables. Stir-fry for ~{2%minutes}, then push to the side of the wok and tip in the egg. Allow to cook undisturbed until almost set, then scramble into the remaining ingredients. Add the meat and prawns and mix in, then tip in the noodles and toss everything together for a couple of minutes, so it is all well combined.

Heap on to a serving plate, top with @coriander{handful}(chopped) and serve immediately.